  "segments": [
    {
      "id": "m23-s001",
      "speakerId": "m23-spk-a",
      "startMs": 0,
      "endMs": 5920,
      "rev": 1,
      "text": "Thanks all. This is the gate review, first model results on the labelled sample."
    },
    {
      "id": "m23-s002",
      "speakerId": "m23-spk-d",
      "startMs": 6170,
      "endMs": 14370,
      "rev": 1,
      "text": "On the held-out set, the model's precision is 0.91 on the three target reason codes. Recall is lower, around 0.78."
    },
    {
      "id": "m23-s003",
      "speakerId": "m23-spk-c",
      "startMs": 14620,
      "endMs": 19400,
      "rev": 1,
      "text": "Explain that to me like I'm the CFO. Which I am."
    },
    {
      "id": "m23-s004",
      "speakerId": "m23-spk-d",
      "startMs": 19650,
      "endMs": 33170,
      "rev": 1,
      "text": "When the model says a dispute is a clear case, it's right nine times out of ten. It misses about a fifth of the clear cases, which then go to a human as today."
    },
    {
      "id": "m23-s005",
      "speakerId": "m23-spk-b",
      "startMs": 33420,
      "endMs": 37060,
      "rev": 1,
      "text": "So nothing gets worse, some things get faster."
    },
    {
      "id": "m23-s006",
      "speakerId": "m23-spk-c",
      "startMs": 37310,
      "endMs": 43610,
      "rev": 1,
      "text": "I'm fine with that, but I don't want the model rejecting anything on its own."
    },
    {
      "id": "m23-s007",
      "speakerId": "m23-spk-b",
      "startMs": 43860,
      "endMs": 47500,
      "rev": 1,
      "text": "Agreed. My analysts should make every final call."
    },
    {
      "id": "m23-s008",
      "speakerId": "m23-spk-a",
      "startMs": 47750,
      "endMs": 53670,
      "rev": 1,
      "text": "So the model flags disputes for review but never auto-rejects. Is that the decision?"
    },
    {
      "id": "m23-s009",
      "speakerId": "m23-spk-c",
      "startMs": 53920,
      "endMs": 56800,
      "rev": 1,
      "text": "That's the decision. Flag, never auto-reject."
    },
    {
      "id": "m23-s010",
      "speakerId": "m23-spk-e",
      "startMs": 57050,
      "endMs": 66010,
      "rev": 1,
      "text": "I'm Yusuf Demir, I lead the disputes platform engineering at Gullwing. For that we'll need a queue the analysts can work from."
    },
    {
      "id": "m23-s011",
      "speakerId": "m23-spk-a",
      "startMs": 66260,
      "endMs": 69140,
      "rev": 1,
      "text": "What would you need to build?"
    },
    {
      "id": "m23-s012",
      "speakerId": "m23-spk-e",
      "startMs": 69390,
      "endMs": 76450,
      "rev": 1,
      "text": "An API that exposes the flagged disputes queue. I'll expose the disputes queue API by June 18."
    },
    {
      "id": "m23-s013",
      "speakerId": "m23-spk-d",
      "startMs": 76700,
      "endMs": 80340,
      "rev": 1,
      "text": "I'll give you the model output schema today."
    },
    {
      "id": "m23-s014",
      "speakerId": "m23-spk-b",
      "startMs": 80590,
      "endMs": 86130,
      "rev": 1,
      "text": "I'll also need reviewer guidelines, so analysts know how to treat a flag."
    },
    {
      "id": "m23-s015",
      "speakerId": "m23-spk-a",
      "startMs": 86380,
      "endMs": 88120,
      "rev": 1,
      "text": "Who writes those?"
    },
    {
      "id": "m23-s016",
      "speakerId": "m23-spk-b",
      "startMs": 88370,
      "endMs": 92770,
      "rev": 1,
      "text": "I will. I'll write the reviewer guidelines by next Tuesday."
    },
    {
      "id": "m23-s017",
      "speakerId": "m23-spk-c",
      "startMs": 93020,
      "endMs": 97800,
      "rev": 1,
      "text": "Then I'm approving the build phase. Send the paperwork to me."
    },
    {
      "id": "m23-s018",
      "speakerId": "m23-spk-a",
      "startMs": 98050,
      "endMs": 101310,
      "rev": 1,
      "text": "Great news. Hana will send it over."
    },
    {
      "id": "m23-s019",
      "speakerId": "m23-spk-b",
      "startMs": 101560,
      "endMs": 108620,
      "rev": 1,
      "text": "Unrelated, but I'm learning Portuguese for a trip, so if I say obrigada by accident, that's why."
    },
    {
      "id": "m23-s020",
      "speakerId": "m23-spk-a",
      "startMs": 108870,
      "endMs": 110230,
      "rev": 1,
      "text": "Ha, noted."
    },
    {
      "id": "m23-s021",
      "speakerId": "m23-spk-d",
      "startMs": 110480,
      "endMs": 116780,
      "rev": 1,
      "text": "One risk, the model was trained on last year's data. Seasonal fraud patterns may shift."
    },
    {
      "id": "m23-s022",
      "speakerId": "m23-spk-c",
      "startMs": 117030,
      "endMs": 119910,
      "rev": 1,
      "text": "Then we review the numbers monthly."
    },
    {
      "id": "m23-s023",
      "speakerId": "m23-spk-a",
      "startMs": 120160,
      "endMs": 123040,
      "rev": 1,
      "text": "Monthly numbers review, noted. Thanks everyone."
    }
  ],
  "note": {
    "version": 1,
    "body": "# Gullwing pilot model review\n\n**Date:** June 4\n**Attendees:** Alex Rivera (Larkspur Labs), Kwame Mensah (Larkspur Labs), Felix Amundsen (Gullwing Payments), Wen Zhao (Gullwing Payments), Yusuf Demir (Gullwing Payments)\n\n## Summary\n\nGate review of the first chargeback automation model on the labelled dispute sample. Felix approved the build phase.\n\n## Results\n\n- On the held-out set, the model's precision is 0.91 on the three target reason codes; recall is around 0.78.\n- In plain terms: when the model calls a dispute a clear case it is right nine times out of ten, and the clear cases it misses go to a human as they do today.\n- The model was trained on last year's data, so seasonal fraud patterns may shift.\n\n## Decisions\n\n- **The model flags disputes for review and never auto-rejects.** Analysts make every final call.\n- **Felix approved the build phase.**\n- Numbers will be reviewed monthly because of the seasonality risk.\n\n## Action items\n\n- **Yusuf Demir** — expose the flagged disputes queue API by June 18. Yusuf leads disputes platform engineering at Gullwing.\n- **Kwame Mensah** — give Yusuf the model output schema today.\n- **Wen Zhao** — write reviewer guidelines for analysts by next Tuesday.\n- **Hana Sato** — send the build-phase paperwork to Felix.\n\n## Notes\n\n- Wen is learning Portuguese for a trip.\n"
  },
